  "result": "I've implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 12 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes all 14 tests (12 new, 2 existing).\n\nHow it works:\n1. It lowercases the text, splits letters from their accent marks, and drops the marks, so \"Tiếng Việt\" becomes `tieng-viet`.\n2. Some letters have no separate accent mark to drop, so a small table converts them: `đ`/`Đ` → `d`. I also added a few other Latin letters of this kind, beyond what you asked for: `ø` → `o`, `ł` → `l`, `ß` → `ss`, `æ` → `ae`, `œ` → `oe`, `þ` → `th`, `ð` → `d`, `ı` → `i`.\n3. Every run of characters other than a–z and 0–9 becomes one hyphen, and hyphens at the start and end are removed.\n4. The slug is cut to 50 characters, and any hyphen left at the end of the cut is removed. So 49 letters followed by a word gives exactly those 49 letters, never 49 letters and a hyphen.\n\nThe tests cover Vietnamese, `đ`/`Đ`, other European accents, the extra letters in the table, collapsing runs of symbols, trimming hyphens, keeping digits, and the length limit. Text with no Latin letters or digits, such as `日本語`, gives an empty string; there's a test for that.",
